<title>GERMANY: EMI says convincing budgetary consolidation needed.</title>
<headline>EMI says convincing budgetary consolidation needed.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Monetary Institute said in its annual report on European economic convergence on Wednesday that a stability pact was no substitute for convincing budgetary consolidation.</p>
<p>The EMI, the forerunner to the future European Central Bank, is responsible for monitoring EU countries' efforts to fulfil the criteria needed to take part in the planned launch of Europe's single currency in 1999.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
